2026-09-01 pending-review | surface: new campaign | axis: container / information hierarchy
  Promoted "New campaign" from a modal to its own route with a two-column layout: numbered
  steps left, a live read-back of the campaign plus a targeting-gate dry run pinned right.
  The modal put the hardest question in the product (name the KIND of organisation) third,
  in a scrolling box, with no room beside it for the two things that help answer it. Ordered
  the steps by difficulty rather than by database column order, so "who are you looking for"
  is now first and largest and the campaign name is third. Not yet seen rendered by a human —
  no browser was available this session, so the layout is reasoned rather than looked at.

2026-09-01 pending-review | surface: new campaign | axis: AI affordance
  Three AI helpers, each placed against the field it helps with rather than gathered into a
  toolbar: "Suggest campaigns" reads the product brief and proposes three aimed at different
  RELATIONSHIPS (customer / partner / press), "Tidy this up" is the existing reframe, and the
  gate dry-run now runs before the campaign exists. Chose suggestion cards over autofill: a
  campaign aimed at something you never read is the failure this whole screen guards against.

2026-09-01 pending-review | surface: shell | axis: scope / access
  Split the app into two surfaces (local owner, shared teammate over a Cloudflare tunnel).
  Chose a positive per-route allow-list over hiding UI, so an endpoint added later is invisible
  to the shared link until someone opts it in. Marked the shared surface permanently in the
  sidebar rather than trusting the URL to communicate it — an identical-looking app is one
  where somebody eventually goes hunting for the mailbox settings and concludes it is broken.

